%N A400435 Integers that can be expressed as the sum of 3 factorials.
%H A400435 Michael B. Porter, <a href="/A400435/b400435.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A400435 49 is in the sequence since 49 = 4! + 4! + 1!.
%o A400435 (PARI) {my(P = sum(n=0, 6, x^(n!)), limit = 2160); print(select(v -> polcoeff(P^3, v) > 0, [1..limit]))}
